ENCRYPTION PROCESS: 
• The encryption utility will be called by the client. This will encrypt all data other than PID and MD and 
post it to the ICICI Bank Infinity site 
• ICICI Bank in turn will decrypt the data by calling the utility and prompt the customer to log in 
• On successful validation of the transaction details, the payment request is then submitted to the backend, 
and the customer’s account gets debited online. A message is displayed to the customer (in an alert box) 
stating the successful status of his payment, and a payment ID is displayed (This payment ID is unique 10 
digit number and is needed as a reference for any communication with the Bank). 
• After the customer makes payment and confirms the transaction the utility is called by ICICI Bank. This 
utility will encrypt all information other than PID and BID and send it back to the client 
• Post successful authentication, the API invokes the return URL – this URL contains the 10 digit payment 
ID as given to the customer. This payment ID (BID) can be used by the payee to generate a verify URL, 
which can be used to confirm status of any payment made – this may be done online or later on as a batch 
verification process. 
