ICICI Net Banking Technical Integration 
Note Internet Banking ICICI Bank Ltd. 
1 
ICICI Bank – Confidential 
INTRODUCTION 
ICICI Direct Debit service through Net banking Gateway enables the customers to make online payments for 
services/ products availed through online merchant websites. The customers having a valid ICICI Bank account 
no., along with a valid Login ID to make use of Retail Internet banking Services through www.icici.bank.in, are 
eligible for Direct Debit online payments. The sections to follow contain the customer facing process for such 
payments and also give an account of the technical integration that is required to set up this functionality, both, at 
the merchant's end and at ICICI Bank. The document also states the details of various parameters to be passed to 
ICICI Bank systems via URL and otherwise for secured transactions. In addition, a brief overview towards 
Payment processing (transfer of funds, payment verification, session time out failures etc.) has also been included. 
CUSTOMER FACING TRANSACTION PROCESS: 
• The customer logs into the website, and adds goods for purchase to his shopping cart. 
• After checking details of his shopping cart, he proceeds to make the payment. 
• He has various options of payment mode (like credit card, cash on delivery, etc.), one of which is “Payment 
through ICICI.Bank.in”. He chooses this option and clicks to continue. 
• The encryption utility will now be called by the shopping mall. This will encrypt all data other than PID 
and MD and post it to the Infinity site. 
• ICICI in turn will decrypt the data by calling the utility and ask the customer to log in. 
• This brings up the icici.bank.in login screen, where he enters his icici.bank.in user ID and login password. 
• If the details entered by the customer are valid, he is taken to the Payment’ screen. This screen displays 
details of the purchase request made by him. 
• The user can choose his debit account and enter some remarks (say, details of purchase that he has made) 
in the ‘Remarks’ field. 
• If the customer accepts the details from the payment screen, and clicks on Continue, the authentication 
screen will be displayed. 
• On successful validation of his transaction details, the payment request is then submitted to the backend, 
and the customer’s account gets debited online. 
• A message is displayed to the customer stating the successful status of his payment, and a payment ID is 
displayed (This payment ID is unique 10 digit number and is needed as a reference for any 
communication with the Bank). The customer is taken back to the Shopping Mall website where he can 
continue shopping. The return URL is invoked which contains the 10 digit payment ID as given to the 
customer. 
• This payment ID (BID) can be used by the payee to generate a verify URL, which can be used to confirm 
status of any payment made – this may be done online or later on as a batch verification process. 
• At any point within icici.bank.in, if a customer wishes not to go ahead with the payment, he has an option 
to return without making the Payment. 
• The payee is credited with all payments made towards him, and a payment report is sent to him on the 
next working day. 
PAYMENTS PROCESS: 
On processing of the payment request the customer's account is debited and a central pooling account is credited. 
The next working day the pooling account is debited for the equivalent amount and the funds are transferred to the 
respective merchant. The following are the main activities involved in transfer of funds to the merchant: 
2 
ICICI Bank – Confidential 
• The Data Centre sends a merchant-wise report of payments made to the Internet Operations Team. The 
report contains details of Payee id, Amount & Account no. of those customers who have effected the 
payment. 
• The report is checked with a Total merchant-wise MIS report generated by the Internet Operations Team 
in the system. This check throws up non-tallied records that are then reversed. 
• For records that get tallied, the Internet Operations Team then generates a TTUM file containing records 
of merchants. 
• On Uploading the TTUM file the Pooling account gets debited and Account Number of Merchant 
(merchant) mapped in the payment server gets credited. 
• Operations Team also sends a MIS regarding the payment received from customers to the merchant on a 
daily basis. 
On receipt of such file, the merchant also checks for failed transactions at their end and send those transactions for 
refund/ reversal the next day as Refunds payment file which will then be processed for settlement. 
REQUIREMENTS (for Payee): 
• The Shopping Mall (payee) first needs to get a valid Payee ID from the bank (for this, the payee essentially 
has to open an account with ICICI Bank for getting credits to his account). 
• The Shopping Mall will create a unique reference number (PRN) and an item code (ITC) for each of 
transactions that happen on his site. Maximum length of the PRN and ITC to be communicated to 
ICICIBank by the payee. 
• He will form a URL, using the parameters mentioned below (except BID), that will be invoked when the 
customer wants to make a payment through ICICI.Bank.in 
